cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this manuscript when using its results or supporting code."
title: "Understanding Nondeterminism: From Witnesses and Structure to Faster SAT"
authors:
  - family-names: Schlesinger
    given-names: Samuel
repository-code: "https://github.com/SamuelSchlesinger/understanding-nondeterminism"
url: "https://github.com/SamuelSchlesinger/understanding-nondeterminism/blob/main/main.pdf"
date-released: 2026-09-05
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  An AI-assisted deep dive from nondeterministic computation paths and shared
  witnesses to an exponential-space SAT and exact-counting algorithm for B2
  circuits. At any fixed positive gap below four gates per input, the algorithm
  saves an exponential factor over exhaustive search. Further results cover
  low-cycle-rank counting, search, lexicographic indexing, exact uniform sampling,
  existential-projection circuit bounds, and witness coverage. Historical priority
  of the precise combined bounds remains unestablished.
